      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Almost 5 years I made this suggestions so thought to comment an update. Since I saw this was updated to being tracked.\n\nThe new earmuffs system works but it is a one-way meaning you can ONLY hear players within the bubble distance that you set. I would love it to work with voice distance / range as well. I feel my WHISPER idea or just voice distance whatever you want to call it could work with the earmuff system. Again being able to change my voice distance in any world would be useful for any club or any social interaction just like IRL. In the real world I can change my voice volume to be lower so I don't disturb other people nearby it's quite useful.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-17T09:10:59.091Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The idea is simple being able to change your voice proximity by clicking a button that allows you to switch between NORMAL and WHISPER mode. Whisper means your voice can only be heard within a few feet and you can only hear players within a few feet as well. Many times I would be in room or a club and hear people across the room. I know maps can reduce or change the voice drop off distance but I feel this universal change would impact the game greatly. Being able to whisper to your friends and being able to hear only the people you are in direct contact with that are face to face with. I would suggest a button that would appear next to the voice meter in the menu just a simple switch from Normal to Whisper. This could also improve RP greatly as well for those individuals that are interested in roleplaying. Many other games have this as an option for roleplaying and social interaction as it can be difficult to hear / talk to someone whos directly in front of you but you hear 10 other people 30 feet away talking.",
